    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d587">

                <pb facs="1050" n="956" xml:id="pg956"/>

                <head>No. 587.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Lothrop.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-03-23"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 23,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 78.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I reply to your No. 100, concerning the
                    confiscation of the two schooners, <hi rendition="#italic">Eiza</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Henrietta</hi> (the subject of recent instructions), by
                    the Russian authorities, that the Department will hold the cases under
                    consideration and await further reports.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
